      "desc:8": "NTM armor protects with two numbers, shown in the tooltip as §eDT/DR§r for each damage type: §6Physical§r, §6Fire§r, §6Explosion§r and §6Energy§r.\n\n§6Damage Threshold (DT)§r is subtracted from every hit first. If a hit is weaker than the DT, it does nothing at all and you hear a §e\"plink\"§r. This makes good armor almost immune to weak, fast attacks.\n\n§6Damage Resistance (DR)§r is a percentage cut from what is left.\n\nArmor-piercing ammunition ignores part of the DT and DR, while some ammo is weaker against armor. A full set often gives extra bonuses on top: night or thermal vision, enemy health bars, hard landings, step assist, extra dashes, built-in Geiger counters or a sealed suit. Read the set\u0027s tooltip.\n\n§3Armor Modification Table§r inserts, claddings and servos add their own DT and DR on top.",
